<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Nearly every key the app needs is a build setting (INFOPLIST_KEY_* in
	     the project), which Xcode merges into the Info.plist it generates.
	     This file is for the keys Xcode has no build setting for.

	     It used to carry UIBackgroundModes/audio for the radio. The app no
	     longer plays the radio, and an app that declares background audio it
	     never plays is a rejection at review, so the key went with it.

	     It lives outside TallinnTasteBuds/ because that folder is a
	     synchronised group: a plist inside it would also be copied into the
	     bundle as a resource.

	     UILaunchScreen is what iOS draws while the app starts, before any of
	     its code has run. Xcode's generated one is empty, which iOS draws in
	     the system background: black on a phone set to dark, and then the
	     app arrived in its cream. LaunchPaper (Assets.xcassets) is the paper
	     of the style a new install opens in, Red, in both appearances, since
	     the app draws that style whatever the phone is set to. Somebody who
	     chose one of the two night styles sees the cream for a moment first:
	     the launch screen is fixed at build time and cannot know. -->
	<key>UILaunchScreen</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIColorName</key>
		<string>LaunchPaper</string>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
